  "description": "A dynamic link library (DLL) designed to facilitate advanced memory operations in Windows environments. Typically used by software that requires direct access to process memory, such as game trainers, cheat engines, debugging tools, or system utilities, memory.dll provides a collection of functions for:\n\n* Reading and writing process memory safely and efficiently\n* Scanning memory for byte patterns (AoB scanning)\n* Allocating and freeing memory in target processes\n* Managing memory protections and access rights\n* Supporting multi-threaded and asynchronous memory operations\n\nIts modular design enables developers to integrate robust memory manipulation features without handling low-level Windows API calls directly. memory.dll is a critical component in applications that require precise control over memory contents for patching, monitoring, or modifying the behavior of other software in real-time.",
